    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "PROPERTY EXPECTED UNIT THRESHOLD RECOMMENDED ANALYTICAL METHODOLOGY DESCRIPTION\r\nMONITORING\r\nFREQUENCY\r\nRECOM\r\nOR REQ\r\nreactive sites on the\r\nbiochar surface and\r\npotentially enhance\r\ndegradation processes.\r\nC-O bonds are more\r\nlabile than C-C bonds.\r\nFurthermore, the\r\nratio is required to verify\r\nthat low ratios\r\ngenuinely reflect a high\r\ndegree of aromaticity,\r\nrather than the presence\r\nof oxygenated aliphatic\r\ncarbon.\r\nsamples per\r\nsampling.\r\nAsh Content\r\n%\r\n(weight/weight)\r\n– ISO 18122 or ISO 1171 or DIN 51719\r\nMeasurement of ash\r\ncontent in biochar is\r\nimportant because it\r\nrepresents the inorganic,\r\nnon-combustible\r\nfraction remaining after\r\ncomplete combustion.\r\nAsh content can\r\ninfluence soil pH,\r\nnutrient availability, and\r\nbiochar’s capacity to\r\nretain water and\r\nnutrients when applied\r\nto soil.\r\nMeasure\r\nevery\r\nproduction\r\nbatch as per\r\nMethod A or\r\nB applicable,\r\nas defined in\r\nSection 8.3.2\r\nof the Biochar\r\nProduction\r\nand Storage\r\nProtocol.\r\nMinimum\r\nnumber of 3\r\nsamples per\r\nsampling.\r\nRequi\r\nBulk Density (< 3 mm\r\nparticle size)\r\nkg m –\r\nISO 17828: 2025 or VDLUFA-method A\r\n13.2.1\r\nThis measurement\r\nstandardizes particle size\r\nto < 3mm to provide a\r\nconsistent metric for\r\ncomparing different\r\nbiochar samples. It is\r\nprimarily used for\r\nresearch and\r\ncharacterization\r\npurposes, as it eliminates\r\nthe variability caused by\r\nparticle size distribution.\r\nBulk density of the <\r\n3mm fraction also\r\nprovides insights into the\r\nporosity and compaction\r\ncharacteristics of the\r\nfiner material.\r\nMinimum\r\nnumber of 3\r\nsamples.\r\nMeasured at\r\nproject\r\nvalidation\r\nunless\r\nfeedstock,\r\nreactor or\r\nprocess\r\nparameters\r\nchange.\r\nRequi\r\nVolatile matter content\r\n(VMC)/ Volatile\r\nCompounds\r\n%\r\n(weight/weight)\r\n- ASTM D1762-84 or DIN 51720: 2001-03 VMC is indicative of the\r\nlevel of carbonisation,\r\nstability, and reactivity of\r\nMinimum\r\nnumber of 3\r\nsamples.\r\nRecom\r\nO/Corg\r\nH/Corg\r\n-3\r\n03/02/2026, 10:56 Biochar Storage in Soil Environments v1.2 — Isometric\r\nhttps://registry.isometric.com/module/biochar-storage-soil-environments/1.2 15/72"
