    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "is the Total Carbon Content of the\r\nbiochar as analysed using the methods described in Table 2.\r\nis the inorganic carbon content of the biochar as\r\nanalysed using the methods described in Table 2.\r\nPlease refer to Section 8.3.1 of the Biochar Production and Storage\r\nProtocol for full guidelines on number of samples required for the\r\nmeasurement of biochar carbon content, .\r\nTotal Carbon Content\r\nCinorg\r\nCbiochar\r\nPlease refer to Section 8.3.1.1 of the Biochar Production and Storage\r\nProtocol for full guidelines on measurement of mass of biochar\r\napplied, .\r\n5.1.2.1\r\nMeasurement of Mass of Biochar Applied\r\nmbiochar\r\nThe method of calculating differs between Option 1 (200\r\nyear durability) and Option 2 (1,000 year durability). Project\r\nProponents must choose which quantification framework (Option 1, or\r\nOption 2, outlined in full below) they wish to use for Crediting their\r\nProject. The choice of quantification framework and corresponding\r\ndurability associated must be clearly outlined in the PDD.\r\n5.1.2.2\r\nCalculation of Fdurable\r\nFdurable\r\nThe quantification framework for determining the CO e for 200-\r\nyear durability biochar is based on the modelling approach set out\r\nby Woolf et al. (2021) . This peer-reviewed paper developed a model\r\nto estimate the amount of carbon remaining in soil over time using a\r\ndecay function. The calculation of requires two inputs: soil\r\ntemperature at the site of deployment ( ) and the biochar\r\nratio. As discussed in Section 1.2, H/C ratio is a proxy\r\nmeasurement of the (poly)aromaticity of a biochar sample .\r\nAdditionally, soil temperature is highly related to microbial and\r\nchemical degradation of biochar with higher temperatures potentially\r\nincreasing mineralisation rates .\r\nAs such, the formula to calculate Fdurable for 200 year durability is:\r\n(Equation 3)\r\nWhere\r\nis the fraction of carbon remaining in durable\r\nstorage after 200 years.\r\n5.1.2.2.1\r\nOption 1: 200 Year Durability\r\n2 stored\r\n15\r\nFdurable\r\nTsoil\r\nH/Corg org\r\n31\r\n9\r\nFdurable,200 = min(0.95, 1 − [c + (a + b ⋅ ln(Tso )) ⋅ il H/Corg])\r\nFdurable, 200\r\n03/02/2026, 10:56 Biochar Storage in Soil Environments v1.2 — Isometric\r\nhttps://registry.isometric.com/module/biochar-storage-soil-environments/1.2 25/72"
    },
