      "type": "text",
      "text": "PARAMETER DESCRIPTION\r\nREQUIRED OR\r\nRECOMMENDED THRESHOLDS\r\nPARAMETER\r\nTYPE UNITS\r\nPROTOCOL OR MODULE\r\nREFERENCE DATA SOURCE\r\nof oxygenated aliphatic\r\ncarbon.\r\nAsh content\r\nMeasurement of ash\r\ncontent in biochar is\r\nimportant because it\r\nrepresents the inorganic,\r\nnon-combustible\r\nfraction remaining after\r\ncomplete combustion.\r\nAsh content can\r\ninfluence soil pH,\r\nnutrient availability, and\r\nbiochar’s capacity to\r\nretain water and\r\nnutrients when applied\r\nto soil.\r\nRequired - Measured\r\n% (weight\r\n/ weight)\r\nSection 3.3 in the\r\nBiochar Storage in Soil\r\nEnvironments Module\r\nAnalytical dete\r\nof ash content\r\nBulk density (<3 mm\r\nparticle size)\r\nThis measurement\r\nstandardizes particle size\r\nto <3 mm to provide a\r\nconsistent metric for\r\ncomparing different\r\nbiochar samples. It is\r\nprimarily used for\r\nresearch and\r\ncharacterization\r\npurposes, as it eliminates\r\nthe variability caused by\r\nparticle size distribution.\r\nBulk density of the <3\r\nmm fraction also\r\nprovides insights into the\r\nporosity and compaction\r\ncharacteristics of the\r\nfiner material.\r\nRequired - Measured kg m .\r\nSection 3.3 in the\r\nBiochar Storage in Soil\r\nEnvironments Module\r\nAnalytical dete\r\nof bulk density\r\nmm fraction of\r\nVolatile matter content\r\n(VMC)/ Volatile\r\nCompounds\r\nVMC is indicative of the\r\nlevel of carbonisation,\r\nstability, and reactivity of\r\nbiochar. A higher VMC\r\nsuggests greater\r\nreactivity, while a lower\r\nVMC means reduced\r\ninteraction with soil\r\ncomponents.\r\nRecommended - Measured\r\n% (weight\r\n/ weight)\r\nSection 3.3 in the\r\nBiochar Storage in Soil\r\nEnvironments Module\r\nAnalytical dete\r\nof level of carb\r\nstability, and re\r\nbiochar\r\n-3\r\n03/02/2026, 10:56 Biochar Storage in Soil Environments v1.2 — Isometric\r\nhttps://registry.isometric.com/module/biochar-storage-soil-environments/1.2 41/72"
