      "type": "text",
      "text": "PARAMETER DESCRIPTION\r\nREQUIRED OR\r\nRECOMMENDED THRESHOLDS\r\nPARAMETER\r\nTYPE UNITS\r\nPROTOCOL OR MODULE\r\nREFERENCE DATA SOURCE\r\ncan be done by\r\ncomparing XPS of in-tact\r\nparticles to Raman/NMR\r\nof pulverised samples\r\nOR XPS of pulverised\r\nand unpulverised\r\nsamples. In either case,\r\nthe sample preparation\r\nshould be specified in\r\nthe PDD. Pulverising\r\nsamples ensures the\r\naverage chemical\r\ncomposition throughout\r\nthe particle is measured,\r\nwhereas the surface\r\ncomposition of in-tact\r\nparticles can be\r\ncharacterised by XPS.\r\ncarbon\r\ndetected\r\nparticles to Ra\r\nof pulverised s\r\nOR XPS of pulv\r\nand unpulveris\r\nsamples. In eith\r\nthe sample pre\r\nshould be spec\r\nthe PDD.\r\nGross calorific value\r\nIndicator of energy\r\ncontent of biochar\r\nRecommended - Measured kJ kg\r\nAnalytical dete\r\nof the total am\r\nheat released w\r\nsample is com\r\ncombusted in a\r\nrich environme\r\nNet calorific value\r\nIndicator of the energy\r\ncontent of biochar\r\nRecommended - Measured kJ kg\r\nAnalytical dete\r\nof the amount\r\nreleased by the\r\ncombustion of\r\nin an oxygen-ri\r\nenvironment ex\r\nthe latent heat\r\nvaporization of\r\nformed during\r\ncombustion.\r\nSpecific surface area\r\nSurface area of biochar\r\napplied to soils\r\nRecommended - Measured m g\r\nSection 3.2 in the\r\nBiochar Storage in Soil\r\nEnvironments Module\r\nMeasurement o\r\nsurface area of\r\napplied to soils\r\nPorosity\r\nPercentage of void\r\nspace in biochar\r\nRecommended - Measured %\r\nSection 3.2 in the\r\nBiochar Storage in Soil\r\nEnvironments Module\r\nAnalytical dete\r\nof the total voi\r\nin biochar, an i\r\nwater adsorpti\r\npotential\r\n-1\r\n-1\r\n2 -1\r\n03/02/2026, 10:56 Biochar Storage in Soil Environments v1.2 — Isometric\r\nhttps://registry.isometric.com/module/biochar-storage-soil-environments/1.2 45/72"
