      "type": "text",
      "text": "PARAMETER DESCRIPTION\r\nREQUIRED OR\r\nRECOMMENDED THRESHOLDS\r\nPARAMETER\r\nTYPE UNITS\r\nPROTOCOL OR MODULE\r\nREFERENCE DATA SOURCE\r\nParticle size distribution\r\nEstimate of the range\r\nand proportion of\r\ndifferent sized particles\r\nwithin a biochar sample\r\nRecommended - Measured\r\n% by size\r\nfraction\r\nSection 3.2 in the\r\nBiochar Storage in Soil\r\nEnvironments Module\r\nMeasurement o\r\nrange and prop\r\ndifferent sized\r\nwithin a biocha\r\nADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS FOR 1,000 YEAR DURABILITY ONLY\r\nRandom reflectance ( )\r\nRandom reflectance is\r\nan indicator of\r\naromaticity, aromatic ring\r\nunit size and\r\ncondensation. A\r\nvalue greater than 2%\r\nhas been proposed as a\r\nbenchmark for\r\nquantifying the\r\npermanent pool of\r\ncarbon in a biochar .\r\nThe frequency\r\ndistribution histogram is\r\nused to decide what\r\nfraction of biochar above\r\nthis benchmark can be\r\nclassified as geologically\r\ninert . This is used to\r\ncalculate .\r\nRequired\r\n> 2 % for\r\ninertinite\r\n(creditable\r\nfraction)\r\nMeasured %\r\nEq. 4 in the Biochar\r\nStorage in Soil\r\nEnvironments Module\r\nAnalytical dete\r\nof random refle\r\nR0 measureme\r\n500 measurem\r\ndifferent bioch\r\nmacerals\r\nReactive Organic\r\nCarbon and Residual\r\nOrganic Carbon (\r\n)\r\nMeasurement of reactive\r\norganic carbon in\r\nbiochar is important\r\nbecause this fraction\r\nrepresents the more\r\nlabile, easily degradable\r\ncomponent of organic\r\ncarbon. Elevated levels\r\nof reactive organic\r\ncarbon can reduce\r\nbiochar’s long-term\r\ncarbon stability, as it is\r\nmore susceptible to\r\nmicrobial decomposition\r\nand mineralization in soil.\r\nRandom reflectance\r\nvalues are subsequently\r\nonly applied to the\r\nresidual, stable fraction\r\nof biochar. This is used\r\nto calculate .\r\nRequired - Measured %\r\nEq. 4 in the Biochar\r\nStorage in Soil\r\nEnvironments Module\r\nRe-pyrolysis of\r\nto achieve sep\r\nthe reactive an\r\norganic carbon\r\nREACTOR MONITORING\r\nR0\r\nR0\r\n11\r\nR0\r\n11\r\nFinert,1000\r\nCnon−reactive\r\nFinert,1000\r\n03/02/2026, 10:56 Biochar Storage in Soil Environments v1.2 — Isometric\r\nhttps://registry.isometric.com/module/biochar-storage-soil-environments/1.2 46/72"
